.TH STOP-MU2EDAQ-APP 1 "2026" "Mu2e DAQ" "Control Room"
.SH NAME
stop\-mu2edaq\-APP \- stop a Mu2e DAQ application under the control room
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B stop\-mu2edaq\-APP.sh
.RB [ \-\-timeout
.IR SECONDS ]
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Standardized stop script for a Mu2e DAQ application, the counterpart to
.BR start\-mu2edaq\-APP (1).
Normally launched by the control room dispatcher
.BR crs\-app (1)
as
.BR "crs\-app stop <app\-id>" .
It reads the pid file written at start, sends
.BR SIGTERM ,
waits up to the timeout for a graceful exit, then escalates to
.B SIGKILL
and removes the pid file. Exiting cleanly when the application is not
running (missing or stale pid file).
.PP
This file is a TEMPLATE: copy it into the application repository and set
the application identity to match the start script.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " SECONDS"
Seconds to wait after
.B SIGTERM
before sending
.BR SIGKILL .
Default 10; also read from
.BR CRS_STOP_TIMEOUT .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CRS_HOME
Control room home (default
.IR ~/controlroom );
locates the pid file under
.IR $CRS_HOME/run
unless
.B CRS_RUN_DIR
overrides it.
.TP
.B CRS_STOP_TIMEOUT
Default graceful\-exit timeout in seconds.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $CRS_HOME/run/<app\-id>.pid
Pid file written by
.BR start\-mu2edaq\-APP (1).
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
0 when stopped or already not running; non\-zero on failure.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR start\-mu2edaq\-APP (1),
.BR crs\-app (1)
